{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-retrofit-county-base",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.84: the `nr-retrofit-county-base` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- Washtenaw County, Michigan, August 2020, weekday, the Industrial sector's NONROAD DIESEL, THC, CO, NOx, methane, SO2, NMHC, VOC, PM10 and PM2.5 running exhaust. It is the un-retrofitted TWIN of `nr-retrofit-county`: the same RunSpec without the user input database that holds the retrofit programs, captured beside it so the retrofit is measured as a ratio.\n\nIT IS THE FIRST RUN THAT SELECTS NONROAD DIESEL AS NONROAD NUMBERS IT. The RunSpec names fuel 23 (Nonroad Diesel Fuel), the nrFuelType ID the MOVES GUI offers for an off-road selection, where every earlier diesel fixture named the onroad fuel 2 that no `nrscc` row carries -- `nr-logging-county` then ran gasoline only and `nr-industrial-county` the whole inventory. Here the packet query returns the sector's seven diesel SCCs, 60 equipment points with a positive Washtenaw population, and the diesel speciation (methane, NMHC, VOC from THC; PM2.5 from PM10) reproduces with them."
  },
